{"id": "955eb667-ef46-406a-9c72-743c139db06e", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T09:28:51.969679", "source": "user", "parent_id": "27980af6-fc84-4865-aef1-5cf9fbbbcd4b", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Please perform an initial inspection and report back with the following three items only (no solution yet): (1) Input/repository inspection — inspect /workspace and summarize what is actually present (e.g., README, code, configs, scripts, data files, manifests, pre-existing OPRO or BBH artifacts). If the repository is empty or unrelated, say so explicitly. (2) Proposed approach — sketch a concrete experimental design that answers: 'Do the optimized instructions discovered by OPRO outperform the baseline instructions (Let's think step by step. and the empty prompt) on BBH tasks?' The sketch should cover: chosen BBH subset(s), how OPRO-discovered instructions will be sourced/treated (re-run vs. reuse published), model(s) and decoding setup, baselines, scoring metric(s) (exact match vs. task-specific), number of trials/seeds, prompt-construction protocol, and statistical comparison plan. This is a design-only deliverable, so execution is not required and should not be claimed as done. (3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties — list the setup choices you are making that are NOT supported by the supplied materials (e.g., which OPRO paper's instruction set to use, specific BBH tasks, model API assumptions, reproducibility constraints). Flag any item where the source intent is genuinely unknown so we can resolve it before locking the design. Do not invent facts about the project; if the repository holds the relevant artifacts, point to the exact files; if it does not, state that the design will rely on publicly available OPRO/BBH materials.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Do the optimized instructions discovered by OPRO outperform the baseline instructions ('Let's think step by step.' and the empty prompt) on BBH tasks?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
